<setup>

  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="-3" to="3" exclude="-1 0 1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="-4" to="4" exclude="-1 0 1 $a$"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="c" from="-5" to="5" step="2" exclude="-1 1 $a$ $b$"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="d" from="2" to="4"/>

  <function name="F" symbolic="true">$a/2*x^2 + $b*x</function>
  <function name="f">$a*x + $b</function>

  <function name="G" symbolic="true">3*$b*x^3 - $c*x^2</function>
  <function name="g">9*$b*x^2 - 2*$c*x</function>

  <function name="H" symbolic="true">$c/(-$d+1)/x^($d-1)</function>
  <function name="h">$c/x^$d</function>

  <selectFromSequence name="p" from="1" to="3"/>
  <number name="q">$p + 1</number>
  <number name="y">$p - 1</number>
 
  
</setup>  

<p>
  Given a function <m>f</m>, we can define the corresponding integral function <m>A</m> using the formula
  <me> A(x) = \int_c^x f(t) \, dt,</me>
  where <m>c</m> is a fixed constant.  If we only have a graph of <m>f</m>, we can determine considerable information about <m>A</m> by thinking about the net-signed area bounded by <m>f</m> on certain intervals.  If we have a basic formula for <m>f</m>, we can often find a formula for <m>A(x)</m> that does not involve an integral sign; we do so by using the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus.
</p>  

<p>
  For each of the following integral functions, find a formula for the function that does not involve an integral by applying the FTC and filling in the provided blanks.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        <m>A(x) = \int_$p^x (<math simplify>$$f(t)</math>) \, dt = </m> 
        <mathInput name="antiD1"/><m> \bigg|_$p^x  </m>
        <answer simplifyOnCompare symbolicEquality forceSmallCheckWorkButton> <award><when>$antiD1=$$F(t)</when></award> </answer> 
      </p> 
      <p> 
        <m>   = </m> <mathInput name="antiD1x"/> <m>-</m> <mathInput name="antiD1a"/>  <m> = </m> <mathInput disabled><math simplify>$antiD1x - $antiD1a</math></mathInput> <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute forceSmallCheckWorkButton matchPartial>
          <award><when>$antiD1x = $$F(x) and $antiD1a = $$F($p)</when></award>
        </answer>
      </p>  
    </li>
    <li>     
      <p>
        <m>B(x) = \int_$y^x <math simplify>$$g(t)</math> \, dt = </m> 
        <mathInput name="antiD2"/><m> \bigg|_$y^x  </m>
        <answer simplifyOnCompare symbolicEquality forceSmallCheckWorkButton> <award><when>$antiD2=$$G(t)</when></award> </answer>
      </p> 
      <p> 
        <m>   = </m> <mathInput name="antiD2x"/> <m>-</m> <mathInput name="antiD2a"/>  <m> = </m> <mathInput disabled><math simplify>$antiD2x - $antiD2a</math></mathInput> <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute forceSmallCheckWorkButton>
          <award><when>$antiD2x = $$G(x) and $antiD2a = $$G($y)</when></award>
        </answer>
      </p>
    </li> 
    <li>
     
      <p>
         <m>C(x) = \int_{$q}^x <math simplify>$$h(t)</math> \, dt = </m> 
        <mathInput name="antiD3"/><m> \bigg|_$q^x  </m>
        <answer simplifyOnCompare symbolicEquality forceSmallCheckWorkButton> <award><when>$antiD3=$$H(t)</when></award> </answer>
      </p> 
      <p> 
        <m>   = </m> <mathInput name="antiD3x"/> <m>-</m> <mathInput name="antiD3a"/>  <m> = </m> <mathInput disabled><math simplify>$antiD3x - $antiD3a</math></mathInput> <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute forceSmallCheckWorkButton>
          <award><when>$antiD3x = $$H(x) and $antiD3a = $$H($q)</when></award>
        </answer>
      </p>
    </li>     
  </ol>   
</p>  